messages.text:
[cngxMenuItemSubmenu] the companion popover ships without [positionTryFallbacks]. Submenus that clip the viewport edge will not flip without a try-fallback chain. Expose the recommended default as a component field and bind it:

  import { CNGX_SUBMENU_TRY_FALLBACKS } from '@cngx/common/interactive';
  protected readonly submenuFallbacks = CNGX_SUBMENU_TRY_FALLBACKS;

  <div cngxPopover [positionTryFallbacks]="submenuFallbacks">
    <!-- submenu items -->
  </div>

[${...}] the native Popover API is not supported in this browser. Install @oddbird/popover-polyfill and import it in your polyfills:

  npm install @oddbird/popover-polyfill
  // polyfills.ts
  import '@oddbird/popover-polyfill';

[cngxPopover] provideFloatingFallback(computePosition) was registered without middleware. Popovers in browsers without CSS Anchor Positioning will clip against the viewport edge because no flip/shift recovery is configured. Pass middleware on registration:

  import { computePosition, flip, shift } from '@floating-ui/dom';

  providers: [
    provideFloatingFallback(computePosition, [flip(), shift()]),
  ],
